Revision history for Perl distribution GlyphaStore

0.1.0 2026-07-19
        - Initial CPAN-ready release of the native wire-protocol v2 client.
        - GlyphaStore::Client with INIT/BIND bootstrap, pipelines, and
          indeterminate mutation outcomes.
        - GlyphaStore::Protocol bidirectional codec and FNV-1a Worker routing.
        - Hot-path performance: native pack 'Q<', zero-copy octet keys,
          integer FNV-1a, buffered sysread, reused IO::Select, and
          execute_worker_pipelines for multi-Worker overlap. Pipeline results
          avoid eager placeholder hashes and materialize each slot once;
          execute_batch reuses its initial routing decision during encoding;
          connected clients reuse the routing identity validated during INIT.
        - Brutal Perl::Critic (severity 1) enforced via .perlcriticrc,
          scripts/test-perl-client.sh, and CI.
        - Packaging installs the normalized tarball into an isolated prefix and
          reruns conformance without access to the distribution source lib/.
        - Request deadlines use CLOCK_MONOTONIC; thread/fork contract documented.
